# Build config. The SDK auto-discovers ./source and ./resources by convention, INCLUDING
# resource qualifiers like ./resources-<device> and ./resources-spa, so pointing at the
# manifest is enough for those.
#
# The TrendCore barrel is consumed BY SOURCE, not as a pre-built .barrel: the bracket form
# points at the barrel's own jungle and the compiler builds it as part of this app. That means
# no extra build step, no binary artifact to version, and editing the barrel takes effect on
# the next build of any consumer. (A plain, unbracketed path would instead mean "a built
# .barrel lives here" -- the compiler rejects mixing the two forms.)
#
# The path is RELATIVE to this file so the repo works from any checkout location.
TrendCore = [../../barrels/trend-core/monkey.jungle]
base.barrelPath = $(TrendCore)

# Launcher icons: each device has its own resources-<device>/drawables/ with a correctly-sized
# icon (auto-discovered by the device qualifier). There is deliberately NO icon in the base
# resources/ -- a base icon would be overridden by every device and the packager would warn.
#
# NOTE: the launcher icons here are PLACEHOLDERS copied from Option J. They show J's speed
# motif, so K is indistinguishable from J in the device's field list. Redesign before publishing.
project.manifest = manifest.xml
